<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Władysław II Jagiełło</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Jogaila</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Władysław II Jagiełło, known in Lithuanian as Jogaila, was Grand Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> who became King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> after marrying <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jadwiga-of-poland">Queen Jadwiga</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-of-krewo">Union of Krewo</a> of 1385. He founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jagiellonian-dynasty">Jagiellonian dynasty</a> and led the joint Polish-Lithuanian victory over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> at Grunwald in 1410. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a> profile treats his union of the two realms as the starting point of the Commonwealth.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/w-adys-aw-ii-jagie-o.jpg" alt="Władysław II Jagiełło" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jogaila_(W%C5%82adys%C5%82aw_II).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
